  "brandingAndStyle": {
    "writingStyle": "The catalogue is organised in ecological terms — \"Biomes\", \"Food Biomes\", \"Wetlands\", \"Ocean\", \"Forest\" — with alliterative naming for the collections themselves (\"Picnic Pals\", \"Mushroom Mayhem\"). Direct address is imperative and exclamatory: \"Discover Slime Story...!\", \"Explore the Picnic Pal collection\". Products are framed as characters to be introduced rather than stock, under the all-caps header \"MEET THE\", and described with a blunt adjective run that keeps \"weird\" as a selling point beside \"soft\" and \"cuddly\".",
    "artStyle": "The brand works entirely in illustration rather than photography, outlined in thick, hand-drawn black strokes, with a wordmark that is hand-lettered in wobbly all-lowercase letterforms rather than set in a stock face. A soft yellow-green anchors the palette against warm browns, oranges and berry reds. Scenes are dense and top-down, packed edge to edge with food and small round characters, painted with soft shading rather than flat fills.",
